> I did originally look at trying to form a URL on submit and then simply just redirect to that.

Yes this is the way to go for now indeed. But you could also completely replace the homepage content and use instantsearch.js on the homepage as if it was a search page.

Maybe what you could try is this:

``` js
var search = instantsearch({
  searchFunction: function() {
    var queryString = search.helper.getStateAsQueryString();
    // redirect to queryString
  },
....
})
```

Let me know how it goes.
